diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d806ba3..1437d33 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -116,3 +116,22 @@ Tests use Python's standard library; the browser test uses installed Chromium,
 not any downloaded browser automation package. Fixtures are cleaned up, and
 browser screenshots/logs are written under ignored `storage/`. `TEST_URL` can
 override the default `http://127.0.0.1:3000` for HTTP/browser tests.
+
+## Question timer
+
+Set **Timer minutes** and **Timer seconds** in **Quiz settings**. Both default to
+0; 0 minutes and 0 seconds disables the timer. The moderator sees an M:SS
+countdown while a question is open; players never see it. Expiry behaves like
+**Finish**, which also remains available early. **Next** starts a fresh timer.
+Deadlines survive reloads and restarts, and the server handles expiry even when
+no moderator browser is connected. Each game snapshots the quiz's timer setting.
+Timers are local settings, not exported content; imported quizzes have no timer.
+
+Timer regressions (the first two run against `bin/serve`; the restart test launches
+an isolated release binary and temporary database):
+
+```sh
+python3 tests/timer.py
+python3 tests/timer_browser.py
+python3 tests/timer_persistence.py
+```
