new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e0514e9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/timers.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Persistent per-question timers
+
+- Preparation quizzes have `timer_minutes` and `timer_seconds`, both nonnegative
+  integers defaulting to zero. Seconds above 59 are accepted as extra duration.
+  Form validation uses checked integer arithmetic; bad settings re-render the
+  entered values without changing the saved quiz. Older title-only clients keep
+  the current timer, just as they keep the prize settings.
+- New games snapshot the combined duration in `games.timer_seconds`. Quiz edits
+  and deletes cannot alter this or any other game snapshot.
+- Opening a question (Start or Next) sets its `opened_at_us` and nullable
+  `closes_at_us` in the same transaction as phase/current/version. A zero duration
+  produces no deadline. GETs and reconnects never write a new opening timestamp.
+- A server task checks deadlines every 100 ms. A single SQLite UPDATE closes only
+  due **current**, **open** questions and increments their game version exactly
+  once. It cannot advance, end, or double-finish a game. It pushes the same phase
+  notification and uses the same result rendering as manual Finish.
+- Requests for state, answers and controls also check expiry under the shared
+  database mutex, so answers at/after the deadline cannot sneak in between worker
+  ticks. Answer acceptance explicitly checks the deadline too. Manual Finish,
+  automatic Finish, and answers are serialized by that mutex. Stale control
+  versions receive fresh state with HTTP 409.
+- Startup closes overdue questions before binding the listener. Unexpired
+  questions resume with their original absolute deadlines. The timer task stops
+  during graceful shutdown, alongside the existing SSE shutdown handling.
+- Only an open moderator state contains `deadline_at_ms` and `server_now_ms`.
+  The browser uses their difference anchored to `performance.now()`, not its
+  potentially misconfigured wall clock, and displays ceiling seconds in M:SS.
+  Countdown ticks update only the timer text; they do not request state or cause
+  server fan-out. Players receive neither field and create no countdown widget.
+  The server, not browser JavaScript, performs Finish.
+- `QuizContents` remains unchanged: exports contain title/questions/options only.
+  Imports use database defaults and ignore any supplied timer settings.
+- Migrations are additive/idempotent. Legacy quizzes and games have zero duration;
+  old open questions with no deadline remain manually controlled.
+
+## Regression coverage
+
+`cargo test --offline --locked` exercises exact deadline boundaries, old-deadline
+isolation after Next, early Finish, zero/legacy behavior, privacy, input overflow,
+and migration idempotence. `tests/timer.py` tests real HTTP/SSE auto-Finish with no
+moderator browser, settings, refresh, imports/exports and all timer modes.
+`tests/timer_browser.py` uses actual Chromium to verify exact labels, ticking and
+M:SS formats, reload, early/automatic Finish, Next, phone privacy and layout.
+`tests/timer_persistence.py` restarts an isolated release server before and after
+expiry to check settings, continued deadlines and startup recovery.
